  "description": "Lycia.Extensions.RabbitMq provides the RabbitMQ transport for the Lycia Saga framework:\n            - RabbitMqEventBus with command/event/response routing over direct and fanout exchanges\n            - Queue, exchange, binding and dead-letter (DLX/DLQ) topology management\n            - Retry and header transport behavior compatible with Lycia middleware\n            - Native TTL + dead-letter based scheduling strategy with delay topology\n            - Management inspection and conditional deletion of scheduling resources\n            - RabbitMQ-specific dependency-injection registration (AddLyciaRabbitMq)",
